{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["For the horses came — and they shook them in the sea. 'And Israel' — had already gone on dry ground through the midst of the sea. 'Then' — 'Miriam the prophetess took…' and so forth. And like it: כאשר צוה ה׳ את משה ויניחהו אהרן לפני העדות למשמרת. And similarly in Jeremiah: כי בא ירמיה אל בית הבור ואל החנויות וישב שם ירמיה ימים רבים וישלח המלך צדקיהו ויקחהו."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "Rashbam reads the verse as three abbreviated clauses, each quoting a fragment of Exodus 15:19 sequentially; the lemmas 'For the horses came,' 'And Israel,' and 'Then' introduce his parsing of the verse's structure. The comparative examples demonstrate that Scripture can telescope a sequence of events into a single verse with each clause advancing the narrative."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:40.359820060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}